The servicing app's Metro 2 furnishing engine (spec §8.1), ported for the
metro2-furnishing environment's grader.

Source       apps/servicing/src/domain/credit-reporting/{metro2,types}.ts
Vendored at  293261b371fe97d2b6b39e1f29ca60dd808ac8fb (apps/servicing/VENDORED_FROM)
Ported       2026-10-21

Each file here is its source byte for byte except its import statements,
and the rewrite is three rules and no more:
  - the kernel's paths (../../kernel/{calendar,money}/<file>.ts) become
    @hm/kernel/{calendar,money} (the same bytes; packages/kernel/VENDORED_FROM);
  - a sibling's ./<file>.ts becomes ./<file>.js;
  - ../boarding/<file>.ts becomes ../../pmi/ported/<file>.js. The FIFO
    ledger both files import (boarding/delinquency.ts) is already ported,
    byte for byte, for the pmi-termination environment, and held there
    (src/pmi/ported/PORTED_FROM); one copy, not two.
metro2.ts's import from ./types.ts spans four lines (10 to 13). Its last
line, `} from "./types.ts";`, is part of the import statement and takes the
same rewrite. Nothing else may be edited: src/__tests__/metro2.test.ts joins
each import statement onto one line, rewrites the original's by these rules,
compares, and compares the rest of each file, and fails on any difference.
Lint and Prettier skip this directory for the reason they skip the vendored
trees.

No file the port needs is ours: the ledger types come with pmi's port.

Not ported: credit-reporting/ops.ts (buildCycle, phpAfterOmission) and
ops-8-3.ts, which import node:crypto and the stateful servicing-requests
service; suppression.ts and bankruptcy/credit.ts (the §8.3 and §14.4
overlays, which v1 does not grade). The conventions the environment runs
the engine under (each month's ledger, an omitted month's carry, the
forbearance entry figures, what counts as a payment in the month) are
restated in src/metro2/grader.ts with the lines they come from.

To take a change from the servicing app, copy the two files again and apply
the same three rewrites.
